Subject: [sshmap fork 0010] the G0/G1 charset designation is honoured in UTF-8 mode (the VT100 special graphics / ACS)

Provenance: sshmap (v1.6.2, ROADMAP task 2) — the colleagues' `mc` report, reproduced on the vendored
            fork first: `printf '\x1b(0q\x1b(B'` left the literal `q` in the grid (measured through
            `TerminalScreen.feed` + `snapshot()`: cell 0 is `'q'`), where xterm paints a horizontal
            line. The cause is stated twice in `pyte/streams.py` itself: `if self.use_utf8: continue`
            before the `define_charset` dispatch of `ESC ( x` / `ESC ) x`, and the same guard for
            SI/SO. The rationale (http://www.cl.cam.ac.uk/~mgk25/unicode.html#term) holds for an
            ISO-2022 ENCODING switch, which is why upstream skips the whole G0/G1 machinery in UTF-8
            mode — but the VT100 special graphics designation is not an encoding switch: it asks the
            terminal to MAP the ASCII letters of a frame onto box-drawing code points, and xterm does
            exactly that in a UTF-8 locale. The tables are already vendored and complete
            (`pyte/charsets.py`: `MAPS["0"] = VT100_MAP`, `MAPS["B"] = LAT1_MAP`), and
            `Screen.draw()` already applies the selected map (`data.translate(...)`) — only the
            designation never arrived.
            Refused alternative: mapping the ACS letters inside OUR canvas instead of in the
            emulator (a second glyph table next to the grid, disagreeing with what `pyte` holds and
            with the `wcswidth` the cells are laid out by); the vendored fork is the ONE owner of
            the emulation, so the fix travels the §4.7 road (patch + MANIFEST).
            Deviation from upstream that this patch accepts and DECLARES: xterm resets the
            designation on a soft reset and on the alternate-screen give-back, which pyte does not
            model at all (`define_charset` has no savepoint of its own) — unchanged here, the state
            stays per screen like every other charset attribute of `Screen`.
Base:       pyte 0.8.2 (PyPI sdist, sha256 in MANIFEST.md), pyte/streams.py (after patches 0001-0009;
            patch 0006 was the last one to touch this file).
Policy:     keep until upstream makes the designation independent of `use_utf8` (it is the same
            "input is Unicode-only" assumption in 0.8.3.dev); `ESC ( B` / `ESC ( 0` keep their
            upstream meaning in a non-UTF-8 stream, `select_other_charset` (`ESC % @` / `ESC % G`)
            and the UTF-8 DECODING of `ByteStream.feed` are untouched.
Applied:    2026-10-03, sshmap v1.6.2.

